Z||000000||Tom88gt||01-14-2000||09:30 AM||||I washed my engine yesterday and now the car won't start.  <P>I used a med (electric, not gas)pressure washer (probably about 1000-1500psi).  I mostly hit the under side of the engine and transaxle.  Just a little from the sides and the top of the transaxle.  <P>I did point the sprayer at the top of the block, just under the distributor (area was greasy) and hit it a couple of times (just a 1/2 bursts, honestly <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>After, the car started and drove home fine (20 min).  I then left about 30 min later and the car stumbled and died when going around a corner 5 min later.  It will not restart and not even fire.  I checked the plug wires, no spark.  The distributor cap/rotor/module/pick-up is clean and dry and all new.<P>I'm thinking maybe I've shorted out the coil or something?  I'll go back this afternoonm and try it again.  Maybe it will have dried off.  Any thoughts?||||reg||11
Z||000001||dogtired||01-14-2000||05:06 PM||||Tom88gt, think I would first check the GAS guage?????    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Sure sounds like something electrical??? But would have thought it to not have started in the first place???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> I am thinking you have a 2.8 just because of the gt behind your name??? If distributor is as dry as you say, I would be looking at the Coil and tach filter,??? <BR>Just some quick thoughts!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by dogtired (edited 01-14-2000).]||||reg||6
